      "message": "If I recall correctly, `ps -o cmd\u003d \"${pid}\"` should return the command for the matching pid and `grep -qE \"(servod|/sbin/init)` return non-zero if any returned lines match either servod or init. I haven\u0027t used `pgrep` much but I\u0027m not sure if there is a way to do this with a single command. `pgrep -v \"(servod|/sbin/init)\"` will return all pids that do not match either of those but I couldn\u0027t find a way to filter that for a given pid (except grepping for the pid, which doesn\u0027t help).\n\nMaybe the previous method was the best way?",
